From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Maxim Stepanov <g.maxim.stepanoff@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 1 Jul 2026 23:33:41 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] acp_thread: coalesce streamed chunks per agent across
 interleaved streams

Concurrently streaming subagents interleave their deltas, so tail-only coalescing shattered every stream into one entry per delta. Coalesce with the most recent entry of the same subagent group (or the parent session) instead: members render inside their card, so the per-group tail is the visually adjacent block, and group-None boundary entries (user messages, root tool calls) still break coalescing by not being assistant messages.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NZwDRUBrLe74CyJXrdLUAy
---
