+        // to coalesce it into an existing assistant entry. qwen streams several
+        // subagents concurrently, so their deltas interleave in arrival order;
+        // scanning only the thread tail would shatter each subagent's stream into
+        // one entry per delta. Instead we coalesce with the most recent entry of
+        // the *same* group (same parent tool call, or both the parent session):
+        // member entries render inside their own subagent card, so that entry is
+        // still the visually-last block of the card even with unrelated entries
+        // in between. Group-`None` boundaries (user messages, root tool calls)
+        // are never `AssistantMessage`s, so they block coalescing across turns
+        // and across a subagent's own tool calls, same as before.
         let classification = self
             .connection
             .subagent_grouping()
